{%- comment -%}
  PG Card Crop: sit the orbs lower in their Best Sellers card.

  The orb photo is five orbs in the upper half with their reflections filling
  the lower half, so in a square card the subject reads as riding high with
  dead weight underneath.

  WHY NOT object-position. pg-home sizes these images `aspect-ratio:1/1;
  object-fit:cover`, and the orb source is 1792x1800 -- essentially square. cover
  is therefore trimming about 4px top and bottom, and object-position can only
  choose between crops that exist. With no overflow there is nothing to shift,
  and the property would silently do nothing.

  WHY NOT a wider box. Giving this image `aspect-ratio:4/3` would create the
  overflow object-position needs, but the Best Sellers row is three cards side
  by side and the wrapper takes its height from the image. One shorter card
  would drop its title and price out of line with the other two.

  So the box stays square and the slack is made instead: scale the image up a
  little, which pushes 7% of its height past each edge of the wrapper (already
  overflow:hidden), then translate down into that slack. The subject moves down
  inside the frame and the reflection is what leaves at the bottom.

  translateY stays under the 7% available per side, so no gap can open at the
  top. The hover rule has to restate the whole transform: pg-home hovers these
  with `transform:scale(1.04)`, which REPLACES rather than adds to a transform,
  so without restating it the image would snap back to centre under the cursor.

  Scoped by href to the orb card alone. The console and wall art photos are
  framed differently and do not want this.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* the orb card only -- pgh-card is an <a>, so its href identifies the product */
  html body #pgh .pgh-card[href*="pokemon-crystal-ball"] .pgh-card-img img{
    transform:translateY(5%) scale(1.14);
  }
  html body #pgh .pgh-card[href*="pokemon-crystal-ball"]:hover .pgh-card-img img{
    /* pg-home's hover replaces the transform outright, so restate it in full */
    transform:translateY(5%) scale(1.18);
  }
</style>
